version deprecated
	Control assignment of channels to external bus timeslots
apifn	sm_config_module_switching
params	sm_config_module_sw_parms configp
	A value obtained from
fnref	sm_open_module
	which indicates the module to configure.
field	tSMModuleId module in
	Controls whether output timeslots should be assigned automatically.
	The value 1 enables automatic assignment, 0 selects assignment
	by the application.
field	tSM_INT auto_assign_out_ts in
	Controls whether input timeslots should be assigned automatically.
	The value 1 enables automatic assignment, 0 selects assignment
	by the application.
field	tSM_INT auto_assign_in_ts in
	The first stream from which output timeslots are to be
	automatically assigned.
field	tSM_INT out_st0 in
	The second stream from which output timeslots are to be
	automatically assigned.
field	tSM_INT out_st1 in
	The lowest numbered timeslot to use for automatic assignment of
	output timeslots.
	This field is ignored.
field	tSM_INT out_base_ts in
	The data encoding used on timeslots automatically allocated
	within this stream.
enumstart	kSMTimeslotType
	Signals encoded with A-law companding.
enum	kSMTimeslotTypeALaw
	Signals encoded with mu-law companding.
enum	kSMTimeslotTypeMuLaw
	Digital data - no companding used.
enum	kSMTimeslotTypeData
enumend	in_type in
	The first stream from which input timeslots are to be
	automatically assigned.
field	tSM_INT in_st0 in
	The second stream from which input timeslots are to be
	automatically assigned.
field	tSM_INT in_st1 in
	The lowest numbered timeslot to use for automatic assignment of
	input timeslots.
	This field is ignored.
field	tSM_INT in_base_ts in
	The data encoding used on timeslots automatically allocated
	within this stream.
enumref	kSMTimeslotType	out_type in
unstruct
	Overrides default or configured assignment scheme used by driver to
	associate channels with timeslots on card external bus.
	The streams which can be used with this call depend on the type
	of Prosody carrier card being used. On the ISA Prosody card, the
	accessible streams are on the external bus (MVIP), while on
	other cards they are special internal streams which are only
	accessible to Prosody and the switch driver.
	<p>
	When a channel is allocated, it can have an associated external
	bus MVIP or SCbus timeslot automatically assigned to it.
	Alternatively, timeslot assignment may be left to the
	application which can call
fnref	sm_switch_channel_output
	or
fnref	sm_switch_channel_input
	following channel allocation to explicitly assign an external
	bus timeslot.
	<p>
	If output channel timeslots for module
ref	module
	are to be assigned by the application through calls to
fnref	sm_switch_channel_output,
	then
ref	auto_assign_out_ts
	must be set to zero.
	<p>
	If output channel timeslots for module
ref	module
	are to be automatically assigned, then
ref	auto_assign_out_ts
	must be set to 1 and the fields
ref	out_st0,
ref	out_st1
	and
ref	out_base_ts
	must be set up to specify the external bus streams and timeslots
	to be assigned.
	<p>
	If SCbus external bus timeslots are to be assigned,
ref	out_st0
	and
ref	out_st1
	should both be set to 24 (the stream assigned to the SCbus) and
ref	out_base_ts
	should be set to the first SCbus timeslot to be assigned for
	this module.
	<p>
	If MVIP external bus timeslots are to be assigned,
ref	out_st0
	and
ref	out_st1
	should be set to DSo stream numbers (0..7) for the first 32 and
	second 32 timeslots assigned, and
ref	out_base_ts
	must be set to zero.
	<p>
	If input channel timeslots for module
ref	module
	are to be assigned by the application through calls to
fnref	sm_switch_channel_input,
	then
ref	auto_assign_in_ts
	must be set to zero.
	<p>
	If input channel timeslots for module
ref	module
	are to be automatically assigned, then
ref	auto_assign_in_ts
	must be
	set to 1 and the fields
ref	in_st0,
ref	in_st1
	and
ref	in_base_ts
	must be set up to specify the external bus streams and timeslots
	to be assigned.
	<p>
	If SCbus external bus timeslots are to be assigned,
ref	in_st0
	and
ref	in_st1
	should both be set to 24 (the stream assigned to the SCbus) and
ref	in_base_ts
	should be set to the first SCbus timeslot to be
	assigned for this module.
	<p>
	If MVIP external bus timeslots are to be assigned,
ref	in_st0
	and
ref	in_st1
	should be set to DSi stream numbers (0..7) for the first 32 and
	second 32 timeslots assigned, and
ref	in_base_ts
	must be set to zero.
	<p>
	The use of automatic timeslot assignment is not recommended.
	It prevents the sharing of a timeslot between multiple
	channels (which is useful when debugging as it permits the
	recording of an input without interfering with normal
	processing of that input). Normally it is trivial to assign
	timeslots explicitly (for example, by deriving the timeslot
	number from some property of a call, such as the port and
	timeslot number of the call).
	<p>
	The use of automatic timeslot assignment is not supported on
	ProsodyS or ProsodyX.
explain
	0
retval
