	Associate event with specific/any channel
apifn	sm_channel_set_event
params	sm_channel_set_event_parms eventp
	The channel with which an event is to be associated.
field	tSMChannelId channel in
	The type of the event to associate.
	One of these values:
	<code>kSMEventTypeReadData</code>,
	<code>kSMEventTypeWriteData</code>, or
	<code>kSMEventTypeRecog</code>.
field	tSM_INT event_type in
	Controls the scope of events: none, one channel, or any channel.
	One of these values:
	<code>kSMChannelNoEvent</code>,
	<code>kSMChannelSpecificEventNonIdle</code>,
	<code>kSMChannelSpecificEvent</code>, or
	<code>kSMAnyChannelEvent</code>.
field	tSM_INT issue_events in
	The event to associate.
field	tSMEventId event in
unstruct
	This call may be used to control read/write and/or recognition
	event notification for channels.
	<p>
	Channel associated events must be allocated through a call to
fnref	smd_ev_create.
	<p>
	In general an application can hibernate in an operating system
	specific way waiting for data activity on specific channels, or
	on any channel.
	<p>
	A channel may have events associated with reading data, writing
	data and recognition. The
ref	event_type
	parameter should be set to the type required as follows:
	<p>
	<table border cellpadding=5>
	<tr> <th>Type</th> <th>Associated with</th> </tr>
	<tr>
		<td>kSMEventTypeReadData</td>
		<td>Recording of data</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td>kSMEventTypeWriteData</td>
		<td>Replay of data, dial completion, tone generation</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td>kSMEventTypeRecog</td>
		<td>Recognition of tone, digit etc</td>
	</tr>
	</table>
	<p>
	To enable channel specific event notification for a particular
	channel, set
ref	channel
	to the required channel,
ref	issue_events
	to <code>kSMChannelSpecificEvent</code>, and
ref	event
	to an operating system specific event handle.
	<p>
	To specify the event to be used when waiting for
	read/write/recognition activity on any channel, set
ref	channel
	to <code>kSMNullChannelId</code>,
ref	issue_events
	to <code>kSMAnyChannelEvent</code>, and
ref	event 
	to an operating system specific event handle. To disable further
	use of this event make the same call but with
ref	issue_events
	set to <code>kSMChannelNoEvent</code>.
	<p>
	To enable &quot;any channel&quot; event notification for a
	particular channel, set
ref	channel
	to the required channel,
ref	issue_events
	to <code>kSMAnyChannelEvent</code>, the
ref	event
	parameter is not used.
	<p>
	To disable read/write/recognition event notification for a
	particular channel, set
ref	channel
	to the required channel, and
ref	issue_events
	to <code>kSMChannelNoEvent</code>.
	<p>
	By default, no events are associated with a channel.
explain
	0
retval
