	Generate a name from an error code
apifn	sm_error_name -noinit char*
params	sm_error_name_parms errp
	The error code whose name is required.
field	tSM_INT code in
	The generated name.
field	char name[80] out
unstruct
	Generates a name for the supplied Prosody error code. The name is
	one of the <a href="error.html">standard names</a>, unless the
	error code is unrecognised, in which case a suitable representation
	is used.
explain
	Returns the address of the
ref	name
	field in the supplied parameter structure. This allows the function
	return value to be used as a parameter to another function call.
	For example:
	<pre>
	printf("Error calling sm_replay_start(): %s\n", sm_error_name(&amp;e));
	</pre>
	<p>
	Since this is never null, it can be safely used immediately.
retval

	Redirect the data received by an input channel to a datafeed
apifn	sm_channel_input_data_redirect
params	sm_channel_input_data_redirect_parms redp
	The channel to redirect the received data on
field	tSMChannelId channel in
	Enables (non-zero) or disables (zero) the redirection of data
field	tSM_INT	enable in
	The datafeed which the received data is passed to when redirected
field	tSMDatafeedId datafeed out
unstruct
	When
ref	enable
	is non-zero, request a datafeed identifier from an input channel that 
	will carry the data usually retrieved through the api (e.g. 
fnref	sm_get_recorded_data
	). This identifer can subsequently be used in a call to any of the
	<code>*_datafeed_connect()</code> functions to connect the input data 
	from the channel to a destination. Note though that the data will be
	raw octets and not audio data, so the destination must be expecting 
	raw octets.	The identifier is valid until the channel is released or 
	this function is called	with
ref enable
	set to zero.
	<p>
	There must be no operation in progress (e.g. record) on the input
	half of the channel when this function is called.
	<p>
	Datafeed connections can only be made between objects allocated
	on the same <code>tSMModuleId</code>.
	<p>
	Requires the modules
modref	datafeed
	and
modref redirect
	to have been downloaded.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

	Provide alternative source data to an output channel
apifn	sm_channel_output_source_datafeed_connect
params	sm_channel_output_source_datafeed_connect_parms outsrcp
	The channel to connect the source to
field	tSMChannelId channel in
	The datafeed supplying the data
field	tSMDatafeedId data_source in
	The number of octets to collect before data is ready
field	tSM_INT threshold in
	The data ready timeout in milliseconds. Zero means no timeout is used.
field	tSM_INT timeout in
unstruct
	Connects a datafeed to an output channel. The output channel
	will use the datafeed as its source of data (e.g. for replay or transmit 
	operations).
	<p>
	The data can be buffered before being made available to the output 
	channel for processing. The buffer will wait until it has either
ref	threshold
	octets of data, or
ref	timeout
	milliseconds have passed since data was last provided to the buffer, 
	before allowing the output channel to process the data. This buffering 
	is repeated if the buffer underruns.
	<p>
	There must be no operation in progress (e.g. replay) on the output
	half of the channel when this function is called.
	<p>
	Datafeed connections can only be made between objects allocated
	on the same <code>tSMModuleId</code>.
	<p>
	Requires the modules
modref	datafeed
	and
modref redirect
	to have been downloaded.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

